# Copy to `.env.local` (development) or set it in the deploy environment.
#
# The origin this site is served from: **https://norsta.ir** in production.
#
# It is read at BUILD time by `lib/site.ts` and is what turns the site's own
# relative paths into the absolute URLs that canonical links, OpenGraph images
# and JSON-LD require — and what robots.txt and sitemap.xml are written against.
#
# Set it in the production environment BEFORE the build: the value is baked into
# the prerendered HTML, so setting it afterwards changes nothing until the next
# build. No trailing slash.
#
# Left unset, any build — `next build` locally with `next start`, or a Vercel
# deployment, production or preview — falls back to `https://norsta.ir`, so no
# canonical link, `og:url`, `twitter:image` or JSON-LD `@id` can ever claim
# localhost or a deployment hostname. Only `next dev` falls back to
# `http://localhost:3000`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://norsta.ir
